# bundles, which is no longer built. The functions keep their names and behavior: hactool's other files only see these
# headers. Two behaviors differ, both corrections: a CBC decrypt now writes its last block (with mbedtls's default PKCS7
# padding that block waited for a cipher_finish whose output hactool discarded), and PSS and PKCS#1 v1.5 signatures are
# checked by OpenSSL's verifier instead of hactool's own decoding. beta NCA0's OAEP keeps hactool's decoding: only its
# private exponent is known, and OpenSSL's RSA decryption needs the public one.
#
# CPM applies it after hactool-decrypted.patch (PATCHES in cmake/dependencies.cmake), and cmake/hactool.cmake checks the
# result. To change it, edit copies of the pristine files, rebuild the hunks with
# `diff -u --label a/<file> --label b/<file>`, and update the hashes in cmake/hactool.cmake.
